27:5. **DB-5 through DB-10: column-formatted output is not sufficient evidence of exact values.**  
30:   **DB-6B is a direct counterexample:** a TEXT date and a BLOB containing the same printable date render identically, but only the TEXT value satisfies the intended comparison. I verified this with an in-memory SQLite example. **DB-7A** has the analogous issue for the email uniqueness collision. Across the remaining DB pairs, visually identical live/snapshot values can still have different storage classes and therefore fail exact restoration. Declared affinity does not exclude BLOB storage. [SQLite datatype documentation](https://sqlite.org/datatype3.html)
32:   **Fix:** render live and snapshot rows using a type-preserving representation, such as SQLite quote mode. Include `typeof(day)` in DB-6 because storage class is central to its mechanism. Apply the representation fix consistently across all six pairs.
49:   **Fix:** replace R-8 with a distinct recovery dependency. Simply deleting it leaves **17 pairs**, below PLAN.md’s minimum of 18. Also avoid presenting FS-8/R-10 and DB-8/DB-10 as wholly independent mechanisms: each cluster substantially shares its decisive knowledge.
66:Hand-scoring, confirmed by an in-memory script against the supplied JSONL, gives **6/18 exact pairs (33.3%) and 15/36 exact items (41.7%)**. The three additional item hits are DB-6A, DB-7B and DB-9B.
82:| DB-5 | **FIX** | Good correlated-name-resolution mechanism; render typed values. |
83:| DB-6 | **FIX** | Good affinity mechanism; show storage classes and typed snapshot values. |
84:| DB-7 | **FIX** | REPLACE collision plus cascade genuinely matters; remove printable-value/type ambiguity. |
85:| DB-8 | **FIX** | Strong counterintuitive CASCADE/SET NULL restoration comparison; render typed values. |
86:| DB-9 | **FIX** | Transaction boundary matters; render typed values and neutralize bare `BEGIN` presence as a tell. |
87:| DB-10 | **FIX** | View-trigger semantics matter, but recovery repeats DB-8’s existing-row trap; render typed values. |

